[statement]
A dependency with a single candidate of a package whose condition will
hold answers no name where that candidate cannot be installed beside the
package, as it answers others
(`a-dependency-of-a-condition-that-will-hold-answers-an-earlier-name`):
`e` 3, the best candidate for `e`, has the condition `f`, which `e` 2
needs, and needs `x`, which only `e` 2 provides. apk takes `e` 3 for `e`
and refuses.

[repository]
P:e
V:3
D:x
i:f

P:e
V:2
D:f
p:x=1

P:f
V:1

[request]
e

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   e-2:
|     conflicts: e-3
|     satisfies: world[e] e-3[x]
|   e-3:
|     conflicts: e-2
|     satisfies: world[e]
refused
